      {
        "source_handle": "P0152",
        "title": "Natural polysaccharides as immune adjuvants to overcome immune checkpoint inhibitor resistance: mechanistic insights, clinical evidence, and translational challenges",
        "year": "2026",
        "doi": "10.3389/fimmu.2026.1914914",
        "paper_id": "43db4adf4e2779233c627e8cd307e2c0ac2ad9c1",
        "material_depth": "",
        "material_status": "resolved",
        "aliases": [],
        "locator": {
          "writer_packet": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\planning\\writer_packets\\Ch5.json",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "card_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\paper_cards\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\format_recovered_reading\\43db4adf4e2779233c627e8cd307e2c0ac2ad9c1\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json"
        },
        "study_summary_A": {
          "approach": "The authors conduct a narrative review synthesizing literature from structural biology, immunology, oncology, and biomanufacturing. They organize the content by: 1) Structural determinants of bioactivity; 2) Four mechanistic axes of ICI sensitization; 3) Clinical and preclinical evidence; 4) Translational bottlenecks (heterogeneity, PK/PD, trial design); 5) Future strategies (AI, synthetic biology, nanodelivery). They compare polysaccharides with mainstream immunostimulants and contextualize findings within Technology Readiness Levels (TRLs).",
          "contribution_and_limits": [
            {
              "contribution": "Provides a comprehensive framework linking polysaccharide structure (ESAR) to immune function and ICI synergy, categorizing mechanisms into four distinct axes.",
              "limits": "As a review, it synthesizes existing data rather than generating new experimental evidence; clinical validation is limited to early-phase/small-sample studies."
            },
            {
              "contribution": "Identifies specific translational bottlenecks (structural heterogeneity, low bioavailability) and proposes advanced technical solutions (AI glycomics, synthetic biology, nanodelivery).",
              "limits": "Proposed solutions like Industry 6.0 integration and AI models are largely theoretical or in early development stages; practical implementation details are not yet established."
            },
            {
              "contribution": "Contextualizes polysaccharides against other adjuvants (CpG, STING agonists, FMT) and defines their niche in terms of safety and tolerability.",
              "limits": "Direct head-to-head comparative clinical data between polysaccharides and these other agents are sparse; comparisons are often based on separate study contexts."
            }
          ],
          "key_findings": [
            {
              "conditions": "Fungal beta-glucans",
              "finding": "Intact triple-helix conformation is essential for Dectin-1 binding and immune activation; extraction-induced disruption abolishes activity."
            },
            {
              "conditions": "Plant/Marine polysaccharides",
              "finding": "C-2/C-3 acetylation or sulfation degree are key determinants of TLR4/MyD88 signaling intensity and ROS scavenging."
            },
            {
              "conditions": "Gut microbiota modulation",
              "finding": "Polysaccharides act as prebiotics to enrich beneficial taxa (e.g., Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and increase SCFA production, which synergizes with anti-PD-1 therapy; effects are microbiota-dependent."
            },
            {
              "conditions": "Clinical evidence",
              "finding": "Early-phase trials show promise (e.g., ORR 21.7% in refractory NSCLC with beta-glucan + envafolimab), but large-scale Phase III RCTs are absent; most strategies remain at TRL 3-5."
            },
            {
              "conditions": "Safety considerations",
              "finding": "Excessive intake of fermentable fibers in dysbiotic models may induce cholestatic liver cancer via SCFA accumulation, highlighting a dose-dependent safety boundary."
            }
          ],
          "paper_kind": "review",
          "problem_or_question": "How can natural polysaccharides be rationally designed and utilized to overcome primary and acquired resistance to ICIs in solid tumors, given their complex structures and variable clinical outcomes?",
          "research_scope": "Natural polysaccharides (from fungi, plants, marine organisms) as immune adjuvants to overcome resistance to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs) in solid tumors. Covers structural biology, molecular mechanisms, preclinical/clinical evidence, translational challenges, and future technological directions.",
          "work_summary": "This review systematically analyzes the potential of natural polysaccharides to enhance the efficacy of ICIs by reversing tumor immune resistance. It dissects the structure-activity relationships (SAR) governing immunomodulation, elaborates on four core mechanisms (TAM repolarization, CD8+ T cell rejuvenation, gut microbiota remodeling, and suppression of tumor-intrinsic escape), and evaluates current clinical translation bottlenecks such as structural heterogeneity and low bioavailability. The paper positions polysaccharides within the broader landscape of combination therapies, compares them with other adjuvants, and proposes a roadmap for precision medicine using AI-driven glycomics, synthetic biology, and multi-layer biomarkers."
        },
